From 8804892f735173086010a7ac5450ae4b6c8a7dcd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stefanoconiglio <33290924+stefanoconiglio@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:33:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 17/19] A thumbnails command: every page as a small PNG, TeX
 typesetting to the end meanwhile

(thumbnails DIR WIDTH HEIGHT) writes each page typeset as DIR/page-N.png,
fitted to WIDTH x HEIGHT in the theme's colours, answering each with
(thumbnail PATH PAGE W H SOURCE LINE), then (thumbnails-done COUNT
FINISHED). Until an empty DIR turns it off, TeX goes on to the
document's end instead of stopping at the page on display, so that every
page comes: an editor's strip of slides.
---
 src/frontend/editor.c | 71 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/frontend/editor.h | 13 ++++++++
 src/frontend/main.c   | 77 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 160 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

